<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Cornwallis, 1st Marquess Cornwallis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1738">1738</a>–<a href="/years/1805">1805</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Lord Cornwallis, Charles Cornwallis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Cornwallis was a British army officer and administrator. As a general in the American War of Independence he was besieged by American and French forces at Yorktown, and his surrender in October 1781 effectively ended the war. He later served as Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, where his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/permanent-settlement">Permanent Settlement</a> of 1793 fixed the land revenue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, and as Lord Lieutenant of Ireland during the rebellion of 1798.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-cornwallis-1st-marquess-cornwallis.jpg" alt="Charles Cornwallis, 1st Marquess Cornwallis" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Gainsborough · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Cornwallis,_1st_Marquess_Cornwallis.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Governor-General <b>Lord Cornwallis</b>, allied with the Marathas and the Nizam of Hyderabad, took Bangalore in 1791 and besieged Srirangapatna, and in the Treaty of Seringapatam of 1792 Tipu ceded about half of his territory, paid a heavy indemnity and handed over two of his sons as hostages.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-mysore-1399-1799">Kingdom of Mysore (1399-1799) · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>British forces under <b>Lord Cornwallis</b> shattered Horatio Gates's army at Camden, South Carolina.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-16">16 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Besieged by American and French forces, <b>Lord Cornwallis</b>'s army of about 8,000 surrendered at Yorktown, Virginia.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-19">19 October in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Grosvenor Square, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. Died in Ghazipur, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.51,-0.15&amp;year=1781" aria-label="Grosvenor Square on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4547 381 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Charles Cornwallis, 1st Marquess Cornwallis"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4997 651h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.51,-0.15&amp;year=1781">What was here in 1781? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
